@* Deliberately NOT the toolkit's default "/profile". Mounting it elsewhere is what exercises
   o.Blazor.ProfilePath in Program.cs — without which the profile-menu item would navigate to /profile and
   404. That was the defect the option was added for, so the sample is where it stays proven. *@
@page "/account"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization

<PageTitle>Profile</PageTitle>

@* The way *in* to demo mode and impersonation. The way *out* is <AccessSimulationBar /> in NavMenu, which
   shows on every page — this card is deliberately not the only exit. *@
<AccessSimulationCard />

<UserProfileView />
